# Debugging loop

A short, safe script for practising the debugger. The loop runs exactly five times and
the script only writes to the output panel.

Suggested breakpoints (line numbers count from the first line of the code block):

- line 4 (`var square = Square(i);`) — a plain breakpoint;
- the same line with the condition `i == 3`;
- line 13 (`var result = value * value;`) — reached with **Step Into** (F11).

```csharp run
var total = 0;
for (var i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
{
    var square = Square(i);
    total += square;
    Console.WriteLine($"i = {i}, square = {square}, running total = {total}");
}

total.Dump("Sum of squares 1..5");

int Square(int value)
{
    var result = value * value;
    return result;
}
```
